{"title":"1996 USAMO Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> be a triangle. Prove that there is a line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/2/9b25f8e64b484493fda944d25cad453423041fe6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l$\" width=\"5\" height=\"12\" /> (in the plane of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />) such that the intersection of the interior of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> and the interior of its reflection <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/2/022948689ac03ea1705a6af78b86d32ae2a369eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A&#39;B&#39;C&#39;$\" width=\"55\" height=\"14\" /> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/2/9b25f8e64b484493fda944d25cad453423041fe6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l$\" width=\"5\" height=\"12\" /> has area more than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/4/7547747b133453d3c209cff6cfbf129aa67a6947.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> the area of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the triangle be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />. Assume <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is the largest angle. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> be the altitude. Assume <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/c/8fcd24129aab8a3bb6a6fd7609f0ab9d69e087bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB \\le AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"80\" height=\"15\" />, so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/1/d11962d3201b0b88774c1494ddbdee73b515809f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD \\le BC/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"100\" height=\"18\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/7/6f724194462e88dea52ef33d373f284d57350017.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD &gt; \\frac{BC}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"85\" height=\"37\" />, then reflect in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/7/4c71f19552a05ee5e2b31e94aff3fb986884bf31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B&#39;$\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is the reflection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/6/616afb88b93f1001a244ab66f8367338512139cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B&#39;D = BD$\" width=\"89\" height=\"14\" /> and the intersection of the two triangles is just <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/a/74a48760ced9fbfbbf84cff69d7d094425db8399.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABB&#39;$\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />. But <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/8/ce86774fa580f735523934272991b222a2418689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BB&#39; = 2BD &gt; \\frac{2}{3} BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"163\" height=\"37\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/a/74a48760ced9fbfbbf84cff69d7d094425db8399.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABB&#39;$\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> has more than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/4/7547747b133453d3c209cff6cfbf129aa67a6947.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/f/e1f796ead620a03f26545fb7900172dd6e92eddd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD &lt; BC/3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"100\" height=\"18\" />, then reflect in the angle bisector of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. The reflection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/9/1090530ae883b627e090bfb5e450ef796febca40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"16\" /> is a point on the segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89fff82bb65d0215e49c8c91cb7c553da52205e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> and not <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />. (It lies on the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> because we are reflecting in the angle bisector. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/f/a7fa11b09e9ec88d605b63d1d5e3c4bfc273b671.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A&#39;C &gt; DC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"89\" height=\"17\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/4/1e47e5355392f6ddce2139b995ade4e5769878f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{CAD} &lt; \\angle{CDA} = 90^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"185\" height=\"13\" />. Finally, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/c/becbdb365486a09d127ff7b568900c49582589b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A&#39;C \\le BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"85\" height=\"16\" /> because we assumed <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/1/2918f7d23f9ee8c04baabad86100d68023ec03f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> does not exceed <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/1/7b1ac662f7ddbbce489953c8b7693848239564aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"14\" />). The intersection is at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/5/79535972e0b7f8bc494e7db8250007a8c5066bd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AA&#39;C$\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />. But  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/d/add14baeb3dc61e0777965d676b73bfa7d5137f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{[AA&#39;C]}{[ABC]} = \\frac{CA&#39;}{CB} &gt; CD/CB \\ge 2/3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"267\" height=\"45\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_USAMO\" title=\"1996 USAMO\">1996 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"1996 USAMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=1996\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1996 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1996 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1996 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1996 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1996 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1996 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1996 USAMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017105536\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.029 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.049 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 223/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1313/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 48/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6272/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.192      1 -total\n 60.73%    8.011      1 Template:USAMO_newbox\n 37.67%    4.969      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:12594:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017105536 and revision id 197634. Ren